-- title:
--   Regularity of non-maximal localisations of a completed tame cover
-- statement:
--   Let $O$ be a regular local ring whose maximal ideal is generated by two elements $\varpi, s$ and whose Krull dimension is $2$, and let $e$ be a positive natural number whose image in $O$ is a unit. Let $C$ be an integrally closed domain which is an $O$-algebra, finite as an $O$-module and with $O$ acting faithfully, and let $G$ be a finite group acting faithfully on $C$ by ring automorphisms, commuting with the $O$-action, with $O$ the ring of $G$-invariants of $C$ (`Algebra.IsInvariant O C G`). Let $\mathfrak n$ be a maximal ideal of $C$ lying over the maximal ideal of $O$, assume that the inertia subgroup $\mathfrak n.\mathrm{inertia}\,G$, viewed inside the stabiliser of $\mathfrak n$ in $G$, has cardinality $e$, and that $\mathfrak n.\mathrm{inertia}\,G$ is cyclic. Let $S$ be a local ring which is a localisation of $C$ at $\mathfrak n$, with compatible $O$-algebra structure, and assume that for every non-maximal prime $\mathfrak q$ of $S$ whose contraction to $O$ does not contain $s$, the algebra $O \to S$ is unramified at $\mathfrak q$. Then for every non-maximal prime $\mathfrak p$ of the $\mathfrak n$-adic completion $\widehat C$ of $C$, the localisation of $\widehat C$ at $\mathfrak p$ is a regular local ring.
--
--   This is the $R_1$ condition for the completed tamely ramified cover $\widehat C$: away from its maximal ideal, $\widehat C$ is regular. It is combined with the corresponding normality input in [`AdicCompletion.isDomain_and_isIntegrallyClosed_of_isInvariant_of_isLocalization_atPrime_of_tame`](thm.html#AdicCompletion.isDomain_and_isIntegrallyClosed_of_isInvariant_of_isLocalization_atPrime_of_tame), which deduces that $\widehat C$ is an integrally closed domain.
